        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/escher/{size}/4865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-09-01T01:41:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Stuntman, Fugue State Parse, Prime Wardens Haka, The Scholar, and XTREME Argent Adept try to bring&nbsp;Challenge Mode Heroic Infinitor back to sanity in the insanity of the Time Cataclysm!</p>\n<p>Infinitor plays almost his entire deck on the first turn. This one's gonna end&nbsp;<em>quick,</em>&nbsp;one way or the other! Good luck!</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Spoiler-free hints:<br>\nYou're only going to last a few turns with the entire manifestation squad in play and invincible, so don't even bother with trying to get your heroes set up. Prioritize deck control and defense, and&nbsp;try to weaken as many manifestations as you can each turn so Infinitor's \"Whispers\" psychic blast can slurp them all up.</p>\n<p>(I got Mint, and while the heroes were at low HP, I didn't feel like it was really badly out of control.)</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:54:14.608Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
