        "id": 233677,
        "name": "KateWalker",
        "username": "TakeWalker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-09-01T13:15:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was kind of surprised my strategy of \"just flip him, forget about Manifestations\" actually paid off! Mint!</p>\n<p>About the only thing you need to do on his front side is drop a few Manifestations so he takes the rest out when he flips. But he's gonna flip, it's pretty much inevitable, so you might as well go with it. I ended with just Haka and Scholar alive, which was in fact both of their faults as Scholar played a Rampage off the top of Haka's deck and ruined half the party. :| But Scholar, as is his wont, was <i>very</i>&nbsp;alive, with three Mortal Forms dealing the final blow.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
